.\" Man page for celeritas.
.TH CELERITAS 1 "2026" "celeritas" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
celeritas \- a minimal terminal emulator with its own window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B celeritas
[\fB\-\-title\fR=\fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-class\fR=\fIINSTANCE\fR[,\fIGENERAL\fR]]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIPROGRAM\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B celeritas
opens a window and runs your shell in it, on a pseudo-terminal. It draws the shell's output with OpenGL and sends your keys back to the shell. Close the window to quit.
.PP
Settings come from a Lua file; see
.B CONFIGURATION
below. Command-line options override the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title =\fINAME\fR
Set the window title. The default is "Celeritas".
.TP
.BR \-\-class =\fIINSTANCE\fR[,\fIGENERAL\fR]
Set the window class, which window managers match rules against. On X11 these are the instance and general names; on Wayland the general name is the app id. With one name, it is used for both. The default is "Celeritas".
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-command " \fIPROGRAM\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]"
Run
.I PROGRAM
with
.IR ARGS ,
instead of the shell. Everything after
.B \-e
is passed to the program, so this option must come last.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the selection to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+V
Paste from the clipboard.
.TP
.B Shift+PageUp, Shift+PageDown
Scroll the scrollback by a page. Not used on the alternate screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Space
Turn vi mode on or off.
.PP
Ctrl\-C and the other keys are sent to the shell. Double-click selects a word, triple-click selects a line, and Alt+drag selects a rectangle. Dragging out a selection also sets the X11 primary selection, which the middle button pastes by default.
.SH VI MODE
Vi mode moves a cursor over the scrollback. While it is on, keys do not reach the shell.
.TP
.B h j k l, arrow keys
Move the cursor.
.TP
.B 0, $, Home, End
Move to the start or end of the line.
.TP
.B g, G
Move to the top or bottom of the scrollback.
.TP
.B PageUp, PageDown
Move by a page.
.TP
.B v
Start a selection at the cursor, or cancel the one being made.
.TP
.B y
Copy the selection and stop selecting.
.TP
.B Escape, i
Leave vi mode.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/celeritas/celeritas.lua
or, if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset,
.IR ~/.config/celeritas/celeritas.lua .
If the file does not exist, celeritas creates it with the default settings on first launch. The file is Lua code that returns a table, grouped into sections. Anything left out uses its default. A file with errors prints a message and falls back to the defaults.
.PP
The file is changed while celeritas runs: it is read again within a second. The font, the window size and whether the window is transparent take effect only after a restart. The
.BR shell ,
.B env
and
.B working_directory
settings apply to the next shell started.
.PP
Colours are written as
.B 0xRRGGBB
or
.BR #RRGGBB .
.PP
The built-in defaults are in the source file
.IR dist/celeritas.lua .
.SS window
.TP
.B title
Window title (default "Celeritas").
.TP
.B decorations
Whether the window has a title bar and borders (default true).
.TP
.B decorations_theme_variant
"Dark" or "Light" window decorations. Unset follows the system.
.TP
.B opacity
From 0.0 to 1.0. Only the background becomes see-through (default 1.0).
.TP
.B padding
A table with
.B x
and
.B y
giving blank space around the grid, in logical pixels (default 0).
.TP
.B dynamic_padding
Share any spare window space evenly around the grid (default false).
.TP
.B class
A table with
.B instance
and
.B general
names, as for
.BR \-\-class .
.TP
.B dimensions.columns, dimensions.lines
The starting size in cells (default 80 by 24). A tiling window manager may resize the window.
.SS font
.TP
.B size
Font size in points (default 14).
.TP
.B normal, bold, italic, bold_italic
Each a table with
.B family
and
.B style
to use a specific face. Unset faces are found from the normal font. Italic text uses the font's own italic face, or else the first installed monospace font that has one. Without any italic face, italic text uses the regular face and bold italic uses the bold face.
.SS colors
.B primary.background
and
.B primary.foreground
set the default colours. The
.B normal
and
.B bright
tables set the eight ANSI colours each. Also
.B draw_bold_text_with_bright_colors
(default true).
.SS cursor
.TP
.B style
"Block", "Underline" or "Beam" (default "Block").
.TP
.B vi_mode_style
The cursor shape in vi mode, or "None" to keep the normal shape (default "None").
.TP
.B thickness
The underline and beam thickness as a fraction of the cell (default 0.15).
.TP
.B unfocused_hollow
Draw a block cursor as an outline while the window is unfocused (default true).
.SS scrolling
.TP
.B history
Lines of scrollback kept; 0 turns it off (default 10000).
.TP
.B multiplier
Lines scrolled per mouse-wheel notch (default 3).
.SS selection
.TP
.B save_to_clipboard
Copy a selection to the clipboard as soon as it is dragged out (default false).
.TP
.B semantic_escape_chars
Characters that end a word for double-click selection. The default is common punctuation and brackets, plus space and tab.
.SS mouse
.TP
.B hide_when_typing
Hide the pointer while typing (default false).
.TP
.B bindings
A list of
.BI "{ mouse = " "\(dqMiddle\(dq" ", action = " ACTION " }"
entries. The only mouse button is "Middle". Actions are
.BR PasteSelection " (the default), " Paste ", and " None .
.SS keyboard
.B bindings
is a list of entries, each
.BI "{ key = " KEY ", mods = " MODS ", action = " ACTION " }"
or
.BI "{ key = " KEY ", mods = " MODS ", chars = " TEXT " }"
.RB ( mods
is optional). A
.B chars
entry sends the text to the shell. Actions are
.BR Copy ", " Paste ", " ScrollPageUp ", " ScrollPageDown ", " ScrollLineUp ", " ScrollLineDown ", " ScrollToTop ", " ScrollToBottom ", " ToggleViMode ", and " None
(swallow the key). Later entries take precedence over the built-in keys.
.SS general
.TP
.B working_directory
Directory the shell starts in (default: where celeritas was started).
.TP
.B live_config_reload
Re-read the file when it changes (default true).
.SS env
A table of extra environment variables for the shell.
.SS shell
The shell to run (default
.BR $SHELL ).
.SS scrolling
See
.B scrolling
above.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
return {
    window = { opacity = 0.9, padding = { x = 8, y = 8 } },
    font = { size = 12 },
    scrolling = { history = 10000 },
    keyboard = {
        bindings = {
            { key = "L", mods = "Control", chars = "\\f" },
        },
    },
}
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell to run, unless
.B shell
is set in the configuration.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the configuration file is kept.
.TP
.B CELERITAS_DEBUG
When set, traces key presses, selection and clipboard use to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/celeritas/celeritas.lua
The configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
